{"video_id":"HWR6cE_hynM","title":"Keynote: The Boring Seams","conference":"sans-ai-summit","language":"en","auto_generated":true,"source":"supa","timing":"exact","word_count":2764,"segments":[{"start":2.64,"duration":2.68,"text":"Good morning."},{"start":4.12,"duration":3.6,"text":"Thank you, Rob. Thank you to the"},{"start":5.32,"duration":4.48,"text":"organizers. Thanks to the AV team."},{"start":7.72,"duration":4.84,"text":"Um I'm glad to be here."},{"start":9.8,"duration":4.0,"text":"Um as he said, I'm Julie Davila. I"},{"start":12.56,"duration":2.76,"text":"currently lead product security at"},{"start":13.8,"duration":3.6,"text":"GitLab."},{"start":15.32,"duration":3.76,"text":"Before that, I've held a number of"},{"start":17.4,"duration":2.96,"text":"different roles across infrastructure"},{"start":19.08,"duration":3.44,"text":"engineering,"},{"start":20.36,"duration":4.36,"text":"software engineering, ran an automation"},{"start":22.52,"duration":3.72,"text":"practice for a little bit at Red Hat,"},{"start":24.72,"duration":3.32,"text":"and even ran my own tech startup for a"},{"start":26.24,"duration":4.16,"text":"couple of years, also in the security"},{"start":28.04,"duration":4.0,"text":"space."},{"start":30.4,"duration":5.48,"text":"But the thing that has shaped the way I"},{"start":32.04,"duration":5.68,"text":"view security more than any job title"},{"start":35.88,"duration":3.16,"text":"is something that stems from a side"},{"start":37.72,"duration":2.52,"text":"interest of mine."},{"start":39.04,"duration":3.52,"text":"And actually has nothing to do with"},{"start":40.24,"duration":4.88,"text":"technology."},{"start":42.56,"duration":4.36,"text":"I've spent a lot of time"},{"start":45.12,"duration":5.12,"text":"studying permaculture."},{"start":46.92,"duration":5.56,"text":"How ecosystems sustain themselves."},{"start":50.24,"duration":3.8,"text":"How soil health determines everything"},{"start":52.48,"duration":5.32,"text":"above it,"},{"start":54.04,"duration":3.76,"text":"even though nobody photographs the soil."},{"start":60.88,"duration":4.28,"text":"In permaculture, there is a principle,"},{"start":63.72,"duration":4.44,"text":"use edges"},{"start":65.16,"duration":5.8,"text":"and value the marginal."},{"start":68.16,"duration":3.96,"text":"You can imagine the boundary between a"},{"start":70.96,"duration":3.48,"text":"forest"},{"start":72.12,"duration":4.0,"text":"and a meadow,"},{"start":74.44,"duration":5.16,"text":"the shoreline"},{"start":76.12,"duration":6.52,"text":"between the water and land."},{"start":79.6,"duration":4.88,"text":"This is where the most activity happens."},{"start":82.64,"duration":3.8,"text":"Where all the growth occurs."},{"start":84.48,"duration":4.48,"text":"But it's also where the system is most"},{"start":86.44,"duration":2.52,"text":"vulnerable."},{"start":89.68,"duration":4.64,"text":"And it's this framing that has really"},{"start":91.56,"duration":4.0,"text":"influenced how I view security today."},{"start":94.32,"duration":2.96,"text":"Because I think the most interesting"},{"start":95.56,"duration":3.24,"text":"security problems"},{"start":97.28,"duration":3.6,"text":"aren't in the components that everyone's"},{"start":98.8,"duration":4.92,"text":"watching."},{"start":100.88,"duration":5.4,"text":"It's in the seams between them."},{"start":103.72,"duration":4.8,"text":"And that's what this talk is about."},{"start":106.28,"duration":5.04,"text":"And I want to start with something that"},{"start":108.52,"duration":2.8,"text":"actually happened."},{"start":112.56,"duration":3.4,"text":"A few weeks before going generally"},{"start":114.2,"duration":3.4,"text":"available with GitLab's Geo agent"},{"start":115.96,"duration":3.88,"text":"platform, we found a pickle"},{"start":117.6,"duration":4.96,"text":"deserialization RCE"},{"start":119.84,"duration":4.76,"text":"um in our systems."},{"start":122.56,"duration":3.72,"text":"We hardened the serializer. We blocked"},{"start":124.6,"duration":3.28,"text":"the fallback paths."},{"start":126.28,"duration":3.48,"text":"Closed the ticket."},{"start":127.88,"duration":4.48,"text":"It was good work."},{"start":129.76,"duration":2.6,"text":"It was thorough."},{"start":134.0,"duration":3.52,"text":"But then, a few weeks after we launched"},{"start":135.8,"duration":3.88,"text":"in January,"},{"start":137.52,"duration":4.12,"text":"the same thing."},{"start":139.68,"duration":3.48,"text":"Same surface."},{"start":141.64,"duration":4.64,"text":"Same layer."},{"start":143.16,"duration":3.12,"text":"But a different attack surface."},{"start":148.68,"duration":4.76,"text":"This is the platform that I'm"},{"start":150.2,"duration":3.24,"text":"responsible for security."},{"start":153.92,"duration":5.2,"text":"But neither incident had anything to do"},{"start":156.72,"duration":4.28,"text":"with the model."},{"start":159.12,"duration":4.2,"text":"There was no prompt injection."},{"start":161.0,"duration":4.16,"text":"There was no jailbreak."},{"start":163.32,"duration":4.56,"text":"The models did exactly what they were"},{"start":165.16,"duration":6.84,"text":"supposed to do."},{"start":167.88,"duration":4.12,"text":"The deserialization path didn't care."},{"start":175.2,"duration":4.76,"text":"And what bothers me the most about these"},{"start":177.0,"duration":5.24,"text":"two incidents isn't that they happened."},{"start":179.96,"duration":4.24,"text":"It's that they represent a broader"},{"start":182.24,"duration":3.88,"text":"a broader trend that I've been observing"},{"start":184.2,"duration":4.4,"text":"in our industry."},{"start":186.12,"duration":6.0,"text":"For the past 2 years or so, the security"},{"start":188.6,"duration":6.4,"text":"community has built tools, frameworks,"},{"start":192.12,"duration":6.24,"text":"and threat models, all largely oriented"},{"start":195.0,"duration":3.36,"text":"around what the model outputs."},{"start":206.6,"duration":4.4,"text":"And it's true"},{"start":208.12,"duration":4.96,"text":"that model security is important."},{"start":211.0,"duration":3.96,"text":"Prompt injection is real."},{"start":213.08,"duration":3.44,"text":"Jailbreaks are real."},{"start":214.96,"duration":4.04,"text":"And in recent recent history, the"},{"start":216.52,"duration":4.04,"text":"research community has made significant,"},{"start":219.0,"duration":3.04,"text":"impressive strides to bring us"},{"start":220.56,"duration":4.36,"text":"collectively forward across these"},{"start":222.04,"duration":4.92,"text":"problem domains."},{"start":224.92,"duration":5.16,"text":"But look at what the field has actually"},{"start":226.96,"duration":3.12,"text":"built in that time."},{"start":230.36,"duration":4.92,"text":"Red teaming frameworks"},{"start":232.72,"duration":4.64,"text":"pointed out what the model outputs."},{"start":235.28,"duration":3.6,"text":"OWASP categories organized around what"},{"start":237.36,"duration":3.52,"text":"the model says,"},{"start":238.88,"duration":5.0,"text":"what it reveals,"},{"start":240.88,"duration":5.76,"text":"how it can be manipulated,"},{"start":243.88,"duration":5.04,"text":"the vendors,"},{"start":246.64,"duration":4.68,"text":"the certifications,"},{"start":248.92,"duration":5.28,"text":"the conference tracks,"},{"start":251.32,"duration":6.04,"text":"all oriented around the most visible,"},{"start":254.2,"duration":4.44,"text":"most discussed part of the stack."},{"start":257.36,"duration":4.0,"text":"The new"},{"start":258.64,"duration":2.72,"text":"and unknown one."},{"start":261.64,"duration":4.36,"text":"And this work is important."},{"start":263.72,"duration":4.08,"text":"It really is, and I believe this room"},{"start":266.0,"duration":5.24,"text":"and the folks listening online"},{"start":267.8,"duration":3.44,"text":"understand this better than most."},{"start":273.2,"duration":5.0,"text":"From 2017 to 2022,"},{"start":276.4,"duration":6.12,"text":"research into AI safety grew by over"},{"start":278.2,"duration":4.32,"text":"300%, a number that only keeps growing."},{"start":282.56,"duration":4.64,"text":"In the history of computing, no other"},{"start":285.48,"duration":3.88,"text":"attack surface has garnered this much"},{"start":287.2,"duration":4.72,"text":"academic attention in such a constrained"},{"start":289.36,"duration":2.56,"text":"time frame."},{"start":294.8,"duration":4.72,"text":"But the challenge with all of this is"},{"start":296.92,"duration":4.6,"text":"that when it comes to complex systems,"},{"start":299.52,"duration":4.44,"text":"failures rarely occur where you're"},{"start":301.52,"duration":3.8,"text":"watching."},{"start":303.96,"duration":4.04,"text":"They occur in the seams between the"},{"start":305.32,"duration":2.68,"text":"components."},{"start":311.84,"duration":3.24,"text":"And the orchestration layers that often"},{"start":313.44,"duration":3.0,"text":"wrap the models that we've all grown"},{"start":315.08,"duration":2.6,"text":"accustomed to"},{"start":316.44,"duration":4.12,"text":"often times haven't been through a"},{"start":317.68,"duration":2.88,"text":"single threat model."},{"start":324.68,"duration":3.4,"text":"I want to take a little bit of a detour"},{"start":326.32,"duration":2.8,"text":"and take us back to the early 20th"},{"start":328.08,"duration":2.8,"text":"century"},{"start":329.12,"duration":4.24,"text":"when physics was at a really interesting"},{"start":330.88,"duration":4.08,"text":"place. It was a little bit chaotic."},{"start":333.36,"duration":4.56,"text":"There were really brilliant people and"},{"start":334.96,"duration":5.08,"text":"amazing discoveries made at the time."},{"start":337.92,"duration":3.96,"text":"There was also a growing list of"},{"start":340.04,"duration":3.8,"text":"conservation laws that nobody could"},{"start":341.88,"duration":3.76,"text":"quite fully explain."},{"start":343.84,"duration":4.56,"text":"You have things like energy is"},{"start":345.64,"duration":5.28,"text":"conserved, momentum is conserved."},{"start":348.4,"duration":4.64,"text":"Angular momentum is conserved."},{"start":350.92,"duration":4.56,"text":"But nobody could quite explain how all"},{"start":353.04,"duration":4.2,"text":"of these things were connected or how to"},{"start":355.48,"duration":4.28,"text":"determine whether a given quantity would"},{"start":357.24,"duration":4.56,"text":"be conserved at all."},{"start":359.76,"duration":3.28,"text":"But then Emmy Noether, working out of"},{"start":361.8,"duration":2.52,"text":"Göttingen"},{"start":363.04,"duration":4.08,"text":"at a time where she couldn't even"},{"start":364.32,"duration":4.6,"text":"lecture under her own name,"},{"start":367.12,"duration":5.0,"text":"made a discovery that changed the"},{"start":368.92,"duration":5.48,"text":"foundations of physics forever."},{"start":372.12,"duration":5.8,"text":"She couldn't hold a formal title,"},{"start":374.4,"duration":3.52,"text":"but she published her proof anyway."},{"start":378.68,"duration":5.08,"text":"Every symmetry in a system corresponds"},{"start":381.52,"duration":3.76,"text":"to a conserved quantity."},{"start":383.76,"duration":3.52,"text":"I'll explain this. It's a little bit"},{"start":385.28,"duration":3.64,"text":"simpler than it sounds."},{"start":387.28,"duration":3.68,"text":"If I were to pick up a ball here today"},{"start":388.92,"duration":4.2,"text":"and drop it,"},{"start":390.96,"duration":4.12,"text":"and then drop it again tomorrow,"},{"start":393.12,"duration":4.76,"text":"the same thing will happen."},{"start":395.08,"duration":6.08,"text":"The physics doesn't care what day it is."},{"start":397.88,"duration":5.52,"text":"This indifference is the symmetry."},{"start":401.16,"duration":3.72,"text":"It's what guarantees that energy will be"},{"start":403.4,"duration":3.64,"text":"conserved."},{"start":404.88,"duration":4.72,"text":"If I roll the ball across the stage here"},{"start":407.04,"duration":4.64,"text":"or I roll it across the stage in Tokyo,"},{"start":409.6,"duration":5.2,"text":"same thing. The physics doesn't care"},{"start":411.68,"duration":3.12,"text":"where where you are."},{"start":415.68,"duration":5.04,"text":"So, what Noether proved was that anytime"},{"start":418.52,"duration":3.68,"text":"the rules are indifferent to something,"},{"start":420.72,"duration":4.92,"text":"there will be a quantity that is"},{"start":422.2,"duration":3.44,"text":"guaranteed to be conserved."},{"start":427.88,"duration":5.36,"text":"So, what this means is that if you can"},{"start":430.6,"duration":4.4,"text":"identify the symmetry in a system, you"},{"start":433.24,"duration":4.0,"text":"can generally, with pretty high degree"},{"start":435.0,"duration":4.44,"text":"of accuracy, predict what that system"},{"start":437.24,"duration":5.32,"text":"will conserve, even in systems that"},{"start":439.44,"duration":3.12,"text":"nobody has studied yet."},{"start":445.36,"duration":4.44,"text":"I want to propose that the same kind of"},{"start":447.28,"duration":4.76,"text":"thing holds true in security."},{"start":449.8,"duration":4.28,"text":"Whenever untrusted data crosses into a"},{"start":452.04,"duration":3.48,"text":"privileged execution boundary,"},{"start":454.08,"duration":2.72,"text":"the same class of failure will be"},{"start":455.52,"duration":2.92,"text":"preserved"},{"start":456.8,"duration":5.56,"text":"across frameworks,"},{"start":458.44,"duration":5.8,"text":"across organizations, different years,"},{"start":462.36,"duration":4.52,"text":"every time,"},{"start":464.24,"duration":2.64,"text":"same outcome."},{"start":470.2,"duration":3.64,"text":"AI security is in pre-Newtonian physics"},{"start":472.08,"duration":3.4,"text":"right now."},{"start":473.84,"duration":3.64,"text":"We've all spent a lot of time"},{"start":475.48,"duration":3.68,"text":"documenting our own set of conservation"},{"start":477.48,"duration":5.04,"text":"laws,"},{"start":479.16,"duration":3.36,"text":"some in this conference this week."},{"start":482.72,"duration":2.92,"text":"But, what we haven't really paid"},{"start":484.16,"duration":3.12,"text":"attention to"},{"start":485.64,"duration":3.04,"text":"is the symmetry that produces all of"},{"start":487.28,"duration":3.28,"text":"them."},{"start":488.68,"duration":4.8,"text":"And that symmetry exists. We just"},{"start":490.56,"duration":2.92,"text":"haven't named it yet."},{"start":497.6,"duration":3.84,"text":"Let me show you what I mean."},{"start":499.72,"duration":3.12,"text":"The orchestration layer is something"},{"start":501.44,"duration":2.48,"text":"that exists on most architecture"},{"start":502.84,"duration":3.04,"text":"diagrams."},{"start":503.92,"duration":3.8,"text":"It's usually a box with some arrows"},{"start":505.88,"duration":4.68,"text":"pointing to the model and everything the"},{"start":507.72,"duration":4.12,"text":"model touches."},{"start":510.56,"duration":3.0,"text":"Whether you build this orchestration"},{"start":511.84,"duration":4.12,"text":"layer yourself because you're at GitLab"},{"start":513.56,"duration":5.4,"text":"or something like this, or you get it"},{"start":515.96,"duration":5.0,"text":"through the platform you've procured."},{"start":518.96,"duration":4.28,"text":"That box is actually a cross-system"},{"start":520.96,"duration":3.92,"text":"trust broker."},{"start":523.24,"duration":3.44,"text":"It oftentimes holds credentials to your"},{"start":524.88,"duration":3.16,"text":"CI pipeline."},{"start":526.68,"duration":2.44,"text":"It usually has access to your source"},{"start":528.04,"duration":4.2,"text":"code"},{"start":529.12,"duration":4.92,"text":"and also your IDE connections."},{"start":532.24,"duration":4.84,"text":"It inherits the trust boundary of every"},{"start":534.04,"duration":5.84,"text":"system that connects to it."},{"start":537.08,"duration":6.04,"text":"And the security posture of the system"},{"start":539.88,"duration":5.16,"text":"oftentimes reflects how it was drawn,"},{"start":543.12,"duration":5.44,"text":"as plumbing,"},{"start":545.04,"duration":3.52,"text":"not as a boundary worth hardening."},{"start":549.88,"duration":3.76,"text":"This trust broker in GitLab is a dual"},{"start":552.04,"duration":3.08,"text":"workflow service."},{"start":553.64,"duration":3.56,"text":"It is a Python and LangGraph"},{"start":555.12,"duration":6.8,"text":"LangGraph-based service that sits at the"},{"start":557.2,"duration":4.72,"text":"heart of our um AI engine."},{"start":562.24,"duration":4.92,"text":"It manages agent state. It orchestrates"},{"start":565.04,"duration":3.88,"text":"agents. It passes credentials from the"},{"start":567.16,"duration":3.76,"text":"execution side"},{"start":568.92,"duration":4.0,"text":"and maintains communication with"},{"start":570.92,"duration":5.12,"text":"developer workstations over long-running"},{"start":572.92,"duration":3.12,"text":"persistent connections."},{"start":576.2,"duration":4.96,"text":"Compromise at this layer is in getting"},{"start":578.4,"duration":4.8,"text":"chatbot to say something it shouldn't."},{"start":581.16,"duration":4.84,"text":"It's a compromise of every agent that"},{"start":583.2,"duration":2.8,"text":"connects to it."},{"start":590.4,"duration":5.64,"text":"The first vulnerability had to do with"},{"start":592.4,"duration":5.64,"text":"how agents resume their work."},{"start":596.04,"duration":4.32,"text":"So, if you have an agent and it needs to"},{"start":598.04,"duration":4.2,"text":"execute a multi-step workflow,"},{"start":600.36,"duration":3.56,"text":"a very important piece of functionality"},{"start":602.24,"duration":4.36,"text":"is that agent's ability to be able to"},{"start":603.92,"duration":5.32,"text":"save where it's at and then be able to"},{"start":606.6,"duration":4.92,"text":"pick up where it left off whenever the"},{"start":609.24,"duration":5.6,"text":"workflow resumes. And that is the"},{"start":611.52,"duration":3.32,"text":"deserialization process."},{"start":617.44,"duration":4.24,"text":"The LangChain library we were using"},{"start":619.76,"duration":3.6,"text":"had a custom deserializer,"},{"start":621.68,"duration":4.28,"text":"which would allow for arbitrary method"},{"start":623.36,"duration":4.96,"text":"calls via JSON with a fallback to"},{"start":625.96,"duration":4.2,"text":"pickle."},{"start":628.32,"duration":4.72,"text":"So, we replaced the deserializer with a"},{"start":630.16,"duration":2.88,"text":"hardened one."},{"start":633.84,"duration":4.0,"text":"We created an explicit allow list of"},{"start":636.36,"duration":4.32,"text":"permitted types"},{"start":637.84,"duration":4.84,"text":"with no fallback paths."},{"start":640.68,"duration":3.72,"text":"And we even submitted a patch upstream"},{"start":642.68,"duration":3.12,"text":"to LangChain to ensure the fix was"},{"start":644.4,"duration":4.8,"text":"present in the library for everybody"},{"start":645.8,"duration":3.4,"text":"that used it going forward."},{"start":650.48,"duration":2.08,"text":"Then,"},{"start":651.4,"duration":2.84,"text":"a few weeks after we launched in"},{"start":652.56,"duration":4.12,"text":"January,"},{"start":654.24,"duration":2.44,"text":"same thing."},{"start":658.28,"duration":4.0,"text":"This time it was in our template"},{"start":659.64,"duration":5.32,"text":"rendering pipeline."},{"start":662.28,"duration":4.44,"text":"User-supplied content would go into the"},{"start":664.96,"duration":4.84,"text":"templating engine."},{"start":666.72,"duration":5.56,"text":"This Jinja 2 that was getting processed."},{"start":669.8,"duration":4.2,"text":"And the deserialization"},{"start":672.28,"duration":3.72,"text":"mechanism could be triggered on"},{"start":674.0,"duration":5.68,"text":"user-supplied checkpoint data,"},{"start":676.0,"duration":5.4,"text":"which could then lead to code execution."},{"start":679.68,"duration":4.56,"text":"Think about that for a moment."},{"start":681.4,"duration":4.24,"text":"Checkpoint data as an attack surface."},{"start":684.24,"duration":3.24,"text":"And this is simply a piece of data that"},{"start":685.64,"duration":4.76,"text":"tells the agent where to pick up its"},{"start":687.48,"duration":2.92,"text":"work that it left off."},{"start":692.16,"duration":5.2,"text":"This time the fix wasn't in the median"},{"start":695.08,"duration":6.24,"text":"patch upstream to a library."},{"start":697.36,"duration":6.08,"text":"It was a process-wide ban on unpickling"},{"start":701.32,"duration":3.32,"text":"combined with a hardened template"},{"start":703.44,"duration":3.88,"text":"sandbox"},{"start":704.64,"duration":5.0,"text":"that would prevent callable methods from"},{"start":707.32,"duration":3.96,"text":"the template context objects from being"},{"start":709.64,"duration":3.8,"text":"executed."},{"start":711.28,"duration":4.84,"text":"We went from fixing a surface"},{"start":713.44,"duration":6.92,"text":"to banning the mechanism."},{"start":716.12,"duration":4.24,"text":"That escalation is the lesson."},{"start":721.64,"duration":6.04,"text":"And this pattern isn't unique to GitLab."},{"start":725.08,"duration":7.32,"text":"All across the AI landscape"},{"start":727.68,"duration":4.72,"text":"the structural relationship between"},{"start":733.12,"duration":3.24,"text":"privileged execution boundaries and"},{"start":734.76,"duration":3.92,"text":"untrusted data"},{"start":736.36,"duration":4.44,"text":"is everywhere."},{"start":738.68,"duration":3.84,"text":"One example is LangChain Core"},{"start":740.8,"duration":3.84,"text":"which dealt with its own critical"},{"start":742.52,"duration":3.88,"text":"severity CVE"},{"start":744.64,"duration":5.0,"text":"which allowed for attacker-influenced"},{"start":746.4,"duration":5.68,"text":"model to steer an AI agent into"},{"start":749.64,"duration":4.16,"text":"executing a malicious payload"},{"start":752.08,"duration":4.96,"text":"which when deserialized could lead to"},{"start":753.8,"duration":5.12,"text":"the leakage of environment variables"},{"start":757.04,"duration":4.96,"text":"and in some cases"},{"start":758.92,"duration":3.08,"text":"um code execution."},{"start":763.36,"duration":5.28,"text":"The failure mode"},{"start":764.76,"duration":3.88,"text":"was in an output field of the model."},{"start":768.68,"duration":4.96,"text":"But the true failure was in the"},{"start":770.0,"duration":3.64,"text":"serialization underneath."},{"start":775.0,"duration":4.88,"text":"MCP MCP remote"},{"start":777.84,"duration":3.84,"text":"another critical flaw."},{"start":779.88,"duration":3.8,"text":"And this is a proxy service that allows"},{"start":781.68,"duration":4.68,"text":"AI applications to communicate with"},{"start":783.68,"duration":4.24,"text":"remote MCP servers."},{"start":786.36,"duration":3.68,"text":"The way it works during its"},{"start":787.92,"duration":3.88,"text":"authorization process is it'll take"},{"start":790.04,"duration":4.4,"text":"server-provided URLs and pass them"},{"start":791.8,"duration":3.92,"text":"through to operating system commands."},{"start":794.44,"duration":3.24,"text":"All you had to do was point this at a"},{"start":795.72,"duration":4.52,"text":"malicious server with a specially"},{"start":797.68,"duration":4.08,"text":"crafted authorization endpoint"},{"start":800.24,"duration":4.68,"text":"and you could effectively own every"},{"start":801.76,"duration":3.16,"text":"machine that connect to it."},{"start":806.76,"duration":3.48,"text":"This is the of vulnerability that could"},{"start":808.24,"duration":4.0,"text":"lead to the full system compromise of a"},{"start":810.24,"duration":3.32,"text":"connecting machine."},{"start":812.24,"duration":4.16,"text":"And it was in a proxy that hardly"},{"start":813.56,"duration":2.84,"text":"anybody was looking."},{"start":819.0,"duration":4.08,"text":"Then you have MCP Inspector."},{"start":821.44,"duration":3.8,"text":"Anthropic's own developer tool for"},{"start":823.08,"duration":4.04,"text":"testing MCP servers."},{"start":825.24,"duration":4.04,"text":"Also critical."},{"start":827.12,"duration":4.24,"text":"In fact, it was a tool used by many to"},{"start":829.28,"duration":6.72,"text":"check the security of their own servers"},{"start":831.36,"duration":4.64,"text":"and it itself became the attack surface."},{"start":838.08,"duration":5.2,"text":"And across all of these incidents, both"},{"start":841.0,"duration":5.24,"text":"internal external,"},{"start":843.28,"duration":4.32,"text":"the cellular motive is the same."},{"start":846.24,"duration":2.52,"text":"Different companies, different"},{"start":847.6,"duration":3.24,"text":"frameworks,"},{"start":848.76,"duration":4.0,"text":"same outcome."},{"start":850.84,"duration":3.0,"text":"And each one of these was a different"},{"start":852.76,"duration":2.76,"text":"team."},{"start":853.84,"duration":4.6,"text":"Each one of these happened during a"},{"start":855.52,"duration":4.08,"text":"different time of the year."},{"start":858.44,"duration":3.56,"text":"But they all shared the same thing in"},{"start":859.6,"duration":2.4,"text":"common."},{"start":862.16,"duration":3.04,"text":"The models did exactly what they were"},{"start":863.88,"duration":3.32,"text":"told."},{"start":865.2,"duration":3.48,"text":"And that's the problem."},{"start":867.2,"duration":3.28,"text":"They were following instructions from a"},{"start":868.68,"duration":4.08,"text":"system"},{"start":870.48,"duration":5.8,"text":"without ever without ever verifying"},{"start":872.76,"duration":5.84,"text":"where the instructions came from."},{"start":876.28,"duration":3.52,"text":"And they all made the same implicit"},{"start":878.6,"duration":3.6,"text":"assumption,"},{"start":879.8,"duration":4.8,"text":"or bet, if you will,"},{"start":882.2,"duration":4.32,"text":"that the seam in between the model and"},{"start":884.6,"duration":5.56,"text":"the system didn't need the same amount"},{"start":886.52,"duration":3.64,"text":"of vetting as the model itself."},{"start":892.12,"duration":3.44,"text":"And if your organization doesn't build"},{"start":893.68,"duration":3.96,"text":"the orchestration layer, cuz that's not"},{"start":895.56,"duration":3.92,"text":"your bread and butter,"},{"start":897.64,"duration":5.24,"text":"and you use something like"},{"start":899.48,"duration":6.2,"text":"Claude, Copilot, N8N, or some other"},{"start":902.88,"duration":2.8,"text":"managed service,"},{"start":905.8,"duration":4.44,"text":"that orchestration layer still exists."},{"start":908.24,"duration":5.6,"text":"You just don't own it."},{"start":910.24,"duration":5.96,"text":"It's written in somebody else's service,"},{"start":913.84,"duration":5.28,"text":"somebody else's trust boundaries,"},{"start":916.2,"duration":2.92,"text":"but with your data."},{"start":921.4,"duration":3.8,"text":"No true would recognize this"},{"start":922.52,"duration":2.68,"text":"immediately."},{"start":925.56,"duration":3.0,"text":"The symmetry is there."},{"start":928.72,"duration":3.64,"text":"It's the same structural relationship"},{"start":930.32,"duration":5.16,"text":"between untrusted data and privileged"},{"start":932.36,"duration":3.12,"text":"execution boundaries."},{"start":935.96,"duration":3.36,"text":"The conservation law holds."},{"start":939.6,"duration":4.24,"text":"Anytime there is symmetry in a system,"},{"start":942.28,"duration":4.16,"text":"the failure modes are what's being"},{"start":943.84,"duration":2.6,"text":"conserved."},{"start":952.72,"duration":6.08,"text":"So, why is this orchestration layer so"},{"start":955.28,"duration":4.88,"text":"often overlooked by security teams?"},{"start":958.8,"duration":3.36,"text":"I want to posit that there's three"},{"start":960.16,"duration":4.68,"text":"high-level reasons."},{"start":962.16,"duration":5.16,"text":"And they compound."},{"start":964.84,"duration":5.4,"text":"The first one is that the most brittle"},{"start":967.32,"duration":5.64,"text":"code in an organization is often not"},{"start":970.24,"duration":4.52,"text":"where your security investment is."},{"start":972.96,"duration":3.8,"text":"I'll give you an example."},{"start":974.76,"duration":4.12,"text":"At GitLab, our primary application is a"},{"start":976.76,"duration":3.88,"text":"Ruby on Rails monolith"},{"start":978.88,"duration":4.36,"text":"with over a decade of security"},{"start":980.64,"duration":4.92,"text":"investment behind it. The processes, the"},{"start":983.24,"duration":3.84,"text":"tools, the scanners."},{"start":985.56,"duration":5.32,"text":"Combine that with the institutional"},{"start":987.08,"duration":3.8,"text":"knowledge of thousands of engineers."},{"start":990.96,"duration":2.68,"text":"The new stack,"},{"start":992.4,"duration":4.68,"text":"Python,"},{"start":993.64,"duration":5.16,"text":"LangChain Jinja2"},{"start":997.08,"duration":4.48,"text":"different framework, different language"},{"start":998.8,"duration":2.76,"text":"ecosystem."},{"start":1003.24,"duration":3.2,"text":"And every organization building AI"},{"start":1004.88,"duration":3.64,"text":"agents today"},{"start":1006.44,"duration":5.24,"text":"has a similar type of system"},{"start":1008.52,"duration":3.16,"text":"with similar types of gaps."},{"start":1013.12,"duration":4.36,"text":"The second challenge is that behavior"},{"start":1015.56,"duration":3.28,"text":"is not in code."},{"start":1017.48,"duration":2.76,"text":"It's in data."},{"start":1018.84,"duration":3.16,"text":"System prompts are stored in the"},{"start":1020.24,"duration":5.68,"text":"database."},{"start":1022.0,"duration":3.92,"text":"Tool configurations live in JSON."},{"start":1026.64,"duration":5.48,"text":"And you cannot grep for behavior the"},{"start":1028.56,"duration":3.56,"text":"same way that you grep a controller."},{"start":1033.2,"duration":3.36,"text":"The attack surface of a of the"},{"start":1034.96,"duration":3.56,"text":"orchestration layer"},{"start":1036.56,"duration":3.44,"text":"is a function of what it accepts and"},{"start":1038.52,"duration":3.44,"text":"what it executes."},{"start":1040.0,"duration":3.96,"text":"Not method signatures, not lines of"},{"start":1041.96,"duration":3.68,"text":"code."},{"start":1043.96,"duration":3.32,"text":"Traditional code review"},{"start":1045.64,"duration":4.4,"text":"security review"},{"start":1047.28,"duration":2.76,"text":"wouldn't catch this."},{"start":1051.56,"duration":2.36,"text":"It's the third one that keeps me up at"},{"start":1053.0,"duration":3.08,"text":"night."},{"start":1053.92,"duration":4.96,"text":"And it's not a vulnerability."},{"start":1056.08,"duration":4.92,"text":"It's a visibility problem."},{"start":1058.88,"duration":4.48,"text":"Your logging probably wasn't built for"},{"start":1061.0,"duration":4.72,"text":"the way agents operate."},{"start":1063.36,"duration":4.0,"text":"With persistent connections"},{"start":1065.72,"duration":4.64,"text":"with how they resume the work off of"},{"start":1067.36,"duration":3.0,"text":"checkpoint data."},{"start":1072.64,"duration":3.84,"text":"And"},{"start":1074.16,"duration":4.48,"text":"our own incidents"},{"start":1076.48,"duration":4.12,"text":"during incident response"},{"start":1078.64,"duration":3.24,"text":"we observed the gap in the telemetry we"},{"start":1080.6,"duration":4.28,"text":"could observe"},{"start":1081.88,"duration":5.76,"text":"and the telemetry we actually had."},{"start":1084.88,"duration":6.4,"text":"That itself became its own work stream."},{"start":1087.64,"duration":3.64,"text":"It's been a long ongoing project."},{"start":1092.48,"duration":4.08,"text":"And something I want to make clear"},{"start":1094.8,"duration":2.84,"text":"is that the absence of evidence in your"},{"start":1096.56,"duration":4.76,"text":"logs"},{"start":1097.64,"duration":5.68,"text":"is not the evidence of absence."},{"start":1101.32,"duration":5.88,"text":"If your telemetry architecture was built"},{"start":1103.32,"duration":5.8,"text":"for a world of web applications and APIs"},{"start":1107.2,"duration":4.72,"text":"it probably wasn't built for the access"},{"start":1109.12,"duration":7.08,"text":"patterns of agents."},{"start":1111.92,"duration":4.28,"text":"The seams are where your logging stops."},{"start":1122.56,"duration":4.6,"text":"Noether didn't set out to prove or to"},{"start":1125.32,"duration":3.76,"text":"explain any particular particular"},{"start":1127.16,"duration":3.84,"text":"conservation law."},{"start":1129.08,"duration":4.8,"text":"She sought to explain the pattern that"},{"start":1131.0,"duration":5.6,"text":"connect connected all of them."},{"start":1133.88,"duration":5.08,"text":"And she found it."},{"start":1136.6,"duration":6.08,"text":"The structural symmetry of a system"},{"start":1138.96,"duration":3.72,"text":"dictates what's conserved."},{"start":1143.52,"duration":4.92,"text":"Break the symmetry"},{"start":1144.88,"duration":3.56,"text":"and the conservation law changes."},{"start":1154.84,"duration":5.08,"text":"Oh, want to propose the same playbook,"},{"start":1157.32,"duration":5.28,"text":"the same idea, but apply it to security."},{"start":1159.92,"duration":4.4,"text":"Not Not because this is simple."},{"start":1162.6,"duration":4.0,"text":"It isn't."},{"start":1164.32,"duration":4.44,"text":"But because across all of"},{"start":1166.6,"duration":4.4,"text":"um all of the incidents that I described"},{"start":1168.76,"duration":4.44,"text":"today, the same patterns hold. We're"},{"start":1171.0,"duration":3.48,"text":"going to walk through them."},{"start":1173.2,"duration":4.0,"text":"The first one is to take a look at"},{"start":1174.48,"duration":4.92,"text":"serialization services."},{"start":1177.2,"duration":4.08,"text":"Every time where untrusted data becomes"},{"start":1179.4,"duration":3.72,"text":"a privileged object. These are your"},{"start":1181.28,"duration":4.88,"text":"checkpoint data stores,"},{"start":1183.12,"duration":3.04,"text":"your tool outputs."},{"start":1190.72,"duration":4.64,"text":"The second are the trust assumptions"},{"start":1192.44,"duration":4.4,"text":"between components."},{"start":1195.36,"duration":3.48,"text":"What does your orchestrator trust"},{"start":1196.84,"duration":4.36,"text":"without verifying?"},{"start":1198.84,"duration":4.72,"text":"The authorization gap we found in our"},{"start":1201.2,"duration":4.6,"text":"own platform"},{"start":1203.56,"duration":4.28,"text":"where"},{"start":1205.8,"duration":4.28,"text":"the scope and permissions implied by the"},{"start":1207.84,"duration":4.48,"text":"UI didn't quite match up to what we"},{"start":1210.08,"duration":3.96,"text":"found in the back end."},{"start":1212.32,"duration":4.52,"text":"Wasn't a flaw introduced by any one"},{"start":1214.04,"duration":4.92,"text":"person intentionally."},{"start":1216.84,"duration":4.76,"text":"It was due to a result of unchecked"},{"start":1218.96,"duration":2.64,"text":"assumptions."},{"start":1221.64,"duration":3.8,"text":"Undeclared trust assumptions are the"},{"start":1223.08,"duration":3.76,"text":"most dangerous kind."},{"start":1225.44,"duration":4.72,"text":"Because they don't show up in your"},{"start":1226.84,"duration":3.32,"text":"traditional security review."},{"start":1230.56,"duration":3.08,"text":"They show up in the seams."},{"start":1236.28,"duration":3.56,"text":"Token scope versus the user mental"},{"start":1238.24,"duration":2.8,"text":"model."},{"start":1239.84,"duration":2.44,"text":"What do your users think they're"},{"start":1241.04,"duration":4.12,"text":"authorizing?"},{"start":1242.28,"duration":5.88,"text":"And what are you actually granting them?"},{"start":1245.16,"duration":5.0,"text":"Divergence between these two at scale"},{"start":1248.16,"duration":5.2,"text":"is a confused deputy problem with an AI"},{"start":1250.16,"duration":3.2,"text":"sized blast radius."},{"start":1256.08,"duration":3.72,"text":"Telemetry coverage versus attack"},{"start":1257.72,"duration":5.24,"text":"surface. Where can an attacker move that"},{"start":1259.8,"duration":3.16,"text":"your logging can't see?"},{"start":1263.12,"duration":4.0,"text":"Every high performance agent that trades"},{"start":1265.0,"duration":4.2,"text":"standard HTTP"},{"start":1267.12,"duration":3.8,"text":"or long running persistent connections"},{"start":1269.2,"duration":4.24,"text":"needs purpose-built telemetry to get the"},{"start":1270.92,"duration":4.04,"text":"same level of visibility."},{"start":1273.44,"duration":4.12,"text":"You should find the gaps before somebody"},{"start":1274.96,"duration":2.6,"text":"else does."},{"start":1280.52,"duration":3.68,"text":"So, we have"},{"start":1282.36,"duration":4.88,"text":"four symmetries"},{"start":1284.2,"duration":3.04,"text":"for conserved risks."},{"start":1288.76,"duration":3.04,"text":"So, what what should you do about this"},{"start":1290.36,"duration":5.08,"text":"when you get back to work, whether it's"},{"start":1291.8,"duration":5.48,"text":"Monday or later on this week?"},{"start":1295.44,"duration":3.16,"text":"Map your orchestration layer before you"},{"start":1297.28,"duration":5.44,"text":"need to."},{"start":1298.6,"duration":4.12,"text":"Every service that manages agent state."},{"start":1302.76,"duration":4.84,"text":"Every place that checkpoint data stored."},{"start":1305.28,"duration":3.84,"text":"Your template rendering pipelines."},{"start":1307.6,"duration":4.2,"text":"Diagram them."},{"start":1309.12,"duration":5.6,"text":"And then ask two questions."},{"start":1311.8,"duration":4.6,"text":"Which of these have been threat modeled?"},{"start":1314.72,"duration":3.36,"text":"And which of these"},{"start":1316.4,"duration":3.24,"text":"fall outside of your standard security"},{"start":1318.08,"duration":3.56,"text":"pipeline?"},{"start":1319.64,"duration":4.2,"text":"You can't answer the question"},{"start":1321.64,"duration":4.88,"text":"or the answer is unsatisfactory, that's"},{"start":1323.84,"duration":2.68,"text":"where you start."},{"start":1330.32,"duration":3.84,"text":"Second, treat serialization like your"},{"start":1332.56,"duration":3.76,"text":"perimeter used to be."},{"start":1334.16,"duration":3.8,"text":"The old faulty assumption"},{"start":1336.32,"duration":3.2,"text":"was to trust the network inside the"},{"start":1337.96,"duration":3.72,"text":"firewall."},{"start":1339.52,"duration":5.24,"text":"The new faulty assumption"},{"start":1341.68,"duration":4.64,"text":"is to trust what the database hands you."},{"start":1344.76,"duration":4.52,"text":"The framework defaults."},{"start":1346.32,"duration":2.96,"text":"The checkpoint data."},{"start":1358.04,"duration":5.28,"text":"And second,"},{"start":1359.52,"duration":6.0,"text":"fix the class, not the instance."},{"start":1363.32,"duration":4.92,"text":"We first replaced the serializer before"},{"start":1365.52,"duration":6.04,"text":"realizing we needed to fix the"},{"start":1368.24,"duration":5.12,"text":"templating engine underneath it."},{"start":1371.56,"duration":2.76,"text":"The fix that mattered was the fix that"},{"start":1373.36,"duration":2.76,"text":"asked,"},{"start":1374.32,"duration":3.52,"text":"\"What is the mechanism that causes this,"},{"start":1376.12,"duration":4.88,"text":"and how do we remove it wholesale from"},{"start":1377.84,"duration":3.16,"text":"the underlying system?\""},{"start":1386.08,"duration":4.32,"text":">> And I want to propose"},{"start":1388.2,"duration":4.84,"text":"that we all stop fixating on the shine"},{"start":1390.4,"duration":5.12,"text":"on the shiny AI and instead audit the"},{"start":1393.04,"duration":2.48,"text":"plumbing."},{"start":1400.0,"duration":3.4,"text":"If you're working on problems similar to"},{"start":1401.64,"duration":3.76,"text":"this, have faced similar challenges in"},{"start":1403.4,"duration":3.48,"text":"your org, or just kind of want to nerd"},{"start":1405.4,"duration":2.92,"text":"out,"},{"start":1406.88,"duration":3.28,"text":"I'm happy to chat."},{"start":1408.32,"duration":4.28,"text":"Come find me."},{"start":1410.16,"duration":2.44,"text":"Thank you."}]}